  "_anchors": "anchors: where a standing role's at points when its dressing set nothing down by that name (town_scenes.gd _anchor). at: heart (the square's middle), place:<key> (towns.gd places; or [x, y, z] when the town has none, else no anchor), works:<key> (works.gd building, facing out of its front); turn: radians off the side the camera looks across (SEEN); out: along the way it faces (a number, {row, or}: the row's own value, or {data: [file, path, fallback]}); r: square (the square's radius) or a number; by: castle or stops, worked out from the town's shape.",
  "anchors": {
    "heart": {"at": "heart", "r": "square"},
    "open": {"by": "open", "cover": true, "within": 0.85}, "seen": {"at": "heart", "r": "square"},
    "beat": {"at": "heart", "r": "square"},
    "streets": {"at": "heart", "r": "square"},
    "market": {"at": "place:market", "r": 0.5},
    "well": {"at": "place:well", "or": [0.4, 0, 0.4], "r": "square"},
    "sept": {"at": "place:sept"},
    "crier": {"at": "place:well", "or": [0.4, 0, 0.4], "out": {"data": ["works", "crier.from_well", 0.35]}},
    "muster": {"at": "place:well", "or": [0.4, 0, 0.4], "turn": 1.0, "out": {"row": "from_well", "or": 0.45}},
    "kin": {"at": "place:well", "or": [0.4, 0, 0.4], "turn": 1.0, "out": {"row": "from_well", "or": 0.45}},
    "forge": {"at": "works:forge", "out": {"row": "forge_out", "or": 0.55}}, "bakery": {"at": "works:bakery", "out": 0.3}, "cooper": {"at": "works:cooper", "out": 0.3}, "weaver": {"at": "works:weaver", "out": 0.3},
    "castle": {"by": "castle"},
    "stops": {"by": "stops"}
  },
  "_dressings": "dressings: each name a standing row's dress may give -> its class (extends town_dress.gd: lays the props, says where its people stand). The director keeps one of each; a dress with no row here is an error, never skipped quietly.",
  "dressings": {"riot": "res://scripts/town_dress/riot.gd", "raid": "res://scripts/town_dress/raid.gd", "doorsteps": "res://scripts/town_dress/doorsteps.gd", "camp": "res://scripts/town_dress/camp.gd", "stalls": "res://scripts/town_dress/stalls.gd", "market_day": "res://scripts/town_dress/market_day.gd", "bonfire": "res://scripts/town_dress/bonfire.gd", "feast": "res://scripts/town_dress/feast.gd", "hot": "res://scripts/town_dress/hot.gd", "gallows": "res://scripts/town_dress/gallows.gd", "grant": "res://scripts/town_dress/grant.gd", "rebels": "res://scripts/town_dress/rebels.gd", "build": "res://scripts/town_dress/build.gd", "dole": "res://scripts/town_dress/dole.gd", "mourning": "res://scripts/town_dress/mourning.gd", "funeral": "res://scripts/town_dress/funeral.gd", "bell": "res://scripts/town_dress/bell.gd", "yards": "res://scripts/town_dress/yards.gd"},
  "_standing": "standing: the town's standing scenes, staged by the director whenever the town is dressed (town_life.gd update: its Life rebuilt as its state turns), for as long as their needs hold, in this order (who comes first takes the room). needs: any of these town states (works.gd's: hunger, feast, levy, war, low, prosperity, grief and a ruling's kind: relief, justice, grant, build; and riot in disorder, grasping under a grasping lord); not: none of them; square: the square's own life (a town of director.square_size or more, or the crown's seat; never in a riot; crowd.json on); crown: the crown's seat only. dress: its dressings (dressings: a class each, extends town_dress.gd) lay the scene's props and say where its people go (anchors). roles: who (a people.gd station; a list taken in turn; or odds {station: share}, the last taking the rest, a share may be by state); age; tint ([r,g,b], or house: the holder's colour as the posted guards wear it); n: how many (a number; [least, most]; by state {base, <state>: n, per_size, most} the first state of works.json priority the town is in; {works: a works.json count}); pairs: n counts pairs; at: the anchor (heart, well, seen, market, sept, crier, muster/kin (from_well out from the well, off the crier's line), forge (forge_out before its front), castle (castle_out from its side facing the square, within castle_within square radii), beat, stops (the square's places and its streets, streets square radii up each), streets, or one a dress names); form round it (town-local game units): at (out ahead, side across), box (out and side ranges), across (a row across at out, gap apart), flank (either side at gap, widening), line (out from it, start then gap; room: gaps in a shoulder's room), rows (rows deep, gaps [deep, across]), ring (round it at its r plus r [from, to], jitter_a radians), arc (centred turn radians off its facing, span, r), knots (knots of knot round the town's edge at r, spread), knots_arc (n knots of knot [fewest, most] apart in an arc either side of the seen side, reach_r square radii out), scatter (spread of its r about it), each (one per anchor point: out, side, chance), brawl (pairs face to face, apart); exact: stand right there (else the nearest open spot within reach); off_centre: kept clear of a fountain; face: anchor, point, ahead (wobble radians), behind, heart (jitter), lead (the scene's first person), mid (their knot), pair, half (half to the heart, the rest anyhow); clips: the first move (in turn; random: drawn; can_play: the first the body can play); post: their npc_mind.gd post (a list in turn); cast_post: who's cast for it (people.gd); watch: armed; arm: a stick for a sword by odds; meta: marks (probes and other scripts find them by); by_day: home at night (works.gd); register: keepers (the stall's keeper, villagers.gd serves at it); blows: a brawl's blows first. does: what a walker does instead of a post (LimboAI tasks in town_scenes.gd, every step by the Mover): beat (a guard pair's beat from a street's mouth past the well to another's, from the castle's gate when it stands by; walk: pace, pause, rest moves, mouth, gate, gate_out, ring), errand (carriers between the stops with a load: loads [move, station, sex, shoulder], street_share; walk: pace, pause, set_down), chase (children; walk: pace, stop share of catches that end in a breather, rest seconds, r square radii, catch), dog (a beast: trot, follow), live (a beast left to its own idle life, animals.gd live: hens pecking by the stalls), cart (the horse and cart's round in along a street to the market and out the other: walk: pace, from, market_in, stop, turn_radius, tail), procession (the funeral: its first walks the dress's round, each after the one before; the row's walk: pace, spacing; a bearer carries the bier). march: a levy's men leaving the muster file by file along the nearest road (needs; every [fewest, most] seconds; file men at spacing; most; pace).",
  "_life": "life (town_life.gd's hands, every dressing's): keeper_back how far behind a stall's counter its keeper stands; lane past a road's verge, ground its travellers keep (nobody stands there); heart the ground round a town's heart every road's travellers pass through; heat past a fire's stones, the step nobody takes; site_shows how far a building site has risen before its building shows.",
  "life": {"keeper_back": 0.07, "lane": 0.06, "heart": 0.2, "heat": 0.06, "site_shows": 0.35}
}
